From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:47:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: drop the vendor -march string

lib/cpu/riscv/cpu.mk asks for -march=rv64imafdcvxthead, which only T-Head's
gcc accepts:

  error: '-march=rv64imafdcvxthead': extension 'xthead' starts with 'x' but
  is unsupported non-standard extension

Both halves have to go, and neither costs anything:

  - 'xthead' is a T-Head toolchain umbrella name for the vendor extensions.
    Nothing in the FSBL uses them through the compiler; the handful of vendor
    instructions are hand-encoded (see the previous patch), so the assembler
    never needs to know the extension exists.

  - 'v' means the 0.7.1 draft vector extension to T-Head's gcc, but RVV 1.0
    to a mainline one.  The C906 implements the draft, not 1.0, so keeping
    'v' would be actively wrong - it would let the compiler emit vector
    instructions this core does not have.  The FSBL has no vector code and
    does not autovectorise at -Os, so dropping it changes no generated code.

zicsr/zifencei are deliberately not added: gcc supplies them implicitly here,
and the FSBL has no explicit fence.i.  OpenSBI does, and needs them spelled
out - that is handled in the build hook, not here.
---
diff --git a/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu.mk b/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu.mk
index bffa5f8..0c1fcc2 100644
--- a/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu.mk
+++ b/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu.mk
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ ASFLAGS +=\
 	$(CPPFLAGS) \
 	-DRISCV \
 	-D__ASSEMBLY__ \
-	-march=rv64imafdcvxthead -mstrict-align \
+	-march=rv64imafdc -mstrict-align \
 	-mcmodel=medany \
 	-mabi=lp64d \
 	-ffreestanding  \
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ ASFLAGS +=\
 TF_CFLAGS += \
 	$(CPPFLAGS) \
 	-DRISCV \
-	-march=rv64imafdcvxthead \
+	-march=rv64imafdc \
 	-mcmodel=medany \
 	-mabi=lp64d \
 	-ffreestanding -fno-builtin -Wall -std=gnu99 \
